@startuml 09-analysis-lifecycle
title Analysis lifecycle (D24-001, D25-001, D25-004)

skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> RUNNING : AnalysisRecorder.begin\n(trigger MANUAL or SCHEDULED,\nidentifiers used, networks)

RUNNING --> COMPLETED : every stage ran,\nnothing unavailable\n(zero Mentions included)
RUNNING --> PARTIAL : some source or classification\nunavailable, rest of the result kept
RUNNING --> FAILED : all sources unavailable,\nor a module failed

COMPLETED --> [*]
PARTIAL --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

state RUNNING : blocks a new start of the same Case (409)\nand a scheduled term (SKIPPED_OVERLAP)\nreport and mentions answer 409
state COMPLETED : terminal, never written again
state PARTIAL : terminal; limitations explain what is missing
state FAILED : terminal; kept in history,\nnever shown as zero findings

note bottom
  A rerun (manual or scheduled) is always a new Analysis with its own id;
  reading an Analysis, its Mentions or its report never reruns it.
  A crash between begin and finish leaves RUNNING (not closed automatically, D25-004).
end note

@enduml
